      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15141205633802815,
        "y0": 0.6783003683544828,
        "x1": 0.39876510715492963,
        "y1": 0.6848814238811863
      },
      "text": "Theyrr soules shelde fro peryle.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2829867042253521,
        "y0": 0.6890705221406896,
        "x1": 0.5016006131830986,
        "y1": 0.6961287451726024
      },
      "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. v. 48, f. 47.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "heading",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07125273239436619,
        "y0": 0.7007200837393104,
        "x1": 0.3003982810140844,
        "y1": 0.7109446250268583
      },
      "text": "PERUR. A kind of cup.",
      "html": null,
      "level": 1,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07206242253521127,
        "y0": 0.7148960843503449,
        "x1": 0.38865045791549274,
        "y1": 0.7240529802068352
      },
      "text": "PERUSE. To examine, or survey.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.09513859154929576,
        "y0": 0.7296239102910346,
        "x1": 0.5016006131830986,
        "y1": 0.784209222900056
      },
      "text": "Monsieur Soubiez having perused the fleet, returned to the king, and told him there waa nothing ready ; and that the mariners and souldiers would not yeeld to goe the voyage till they were paid their arrears. MS. HarU 383.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07287211267605634,
        "y0": 0.7909351447751725,
        "x1": 0.3748832964507043,
        "y1": 0.8001338052649877
      },
      "text": "PERVEY. To provide. (^.-A^.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07287211267605634,
        "y0": 0.8041989941931035,
        "x1": 0.4817583465915491,
        "y1": 0.813543830899556
      },
      "text": "PERVINKE. The herb periwinkle. {A.-S.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07287211267605634,
        "y0": 0.8171662203986207,
        "x1": 0.44331021025352096,
        "y1": 0.8502365901518557
      },
      "text": "PERYE. A pear-tree. (A.-N.) But for hur lorde sche durste not done. That sate benethe and pleyed hym merye.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11254692957746477,
        "y0": 0.8556963778593103,
        "x1": 0.36314117002816904,
        "y1": 0.8616896027414375
      },
      "text": "Before the towre undur a perye.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.27772371830985915,
        "y0": 0.8667229479489655,
        "x1": 0.5003852682816902,
        "y1": 0.873490558740659
      },
      "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. ii. 38, f. 141.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "heading",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07287211267605634,
        "y0": 0.8786888075324139,
        "x1": 0.337230275830986,
        "y1": 0.8875342088320224
      },
      "text": "PERYSSE. Pears. {A.-N.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": 1,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.13238433802816899,
        "y0": 0.8915536059806896,
        "x1": 0.4121387592112674,
        "y1": 0.8988763383569937
      },
      "text": "Then was the tre ful of ripe perysse,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.13319402816901407,
        "y0": 0.9035047714331035,
        "x1": 0.32428737892957743,
        "y1": 0.910756155894144
      },
      "text": "And began down to falle.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07408664788732393,
        "y0": 0.9149198761531034,
        "x1": 0.5007868745915494,
        "y1": 0.9364943976656981
      },
      "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. v. 48, f. 114. PESANE. A gorget of mail or plate attached to the helmet. \" A pesane and a paunsone,\" MS. Morte Arthure, f. 89.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5190113802816901,
        "y0": 0.09734701885931042,
        "x1": 0.9497584383098588,
        "y1": 0.14618408332602825
      },
      "text": "PESATE. Is when a managed horse rises handsomely before and upon his haunches, and ax the same time bends hisfore-legs up tohisbody. PESE. (1) Peace. Perceval 980, 981.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.15125199005379317,
        "x1": 0.7473407612394367,
        "y1": 0.1602067922449427
      },
      "text": "(2) To sooth ; to appease.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5979561690140844,
        "y0": 0.1648171757089656,
        "x1": 0.8857977753239435,
        "y1": 0.17087784238884496
      },
      "text": "Tylle y be sewre of youre hartys ese.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5979561690140844,
        "y0": 0.17626700615448276,
        "x1": 0.8902583583098594,
        "y1": 0.18285537706149013
      },
      "text": "Nothing but hit may my grevys pese.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7384374084507042,
        "y0": 0.18803286696827595,
        "x1": 0.9493649289014083,
        "y1": 0.19509109000018873
      },
      "text": "MS. Cantab. Ff. i. G. f. 132.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5194162253521126,
        "y0": 0.19927771800275867,
        "x1": 0.9501729996619718,
        "y1": 0.2614415932234177
      },
      "text": "PESEN. Peas. This is the common early form of the word, and occurs in Chaucer, Legende of Good Women, 648. Holloway gives the following couplet, as seen lately on a board in a pea-field in Berkshire",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5392536338028169,
        "y0": 0.2663982437393104,
        "x1": 0.920616070760563,
        "y1": 0.2849867616805878
      },
      "text": "Shut the gate after you, I'll tell you the reason. Because the pigs shouldn't get into the peason.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5404681690140845,
        "y0": 0.29249405901931036,
        "x1": 0.9493657385915493,
        "y1": 0.31397616432514897
      },
      "text": "Ben Jonson has made the same words rhyme in his 133d epigram.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5396584788732394,
        "y0": 0.31879817413793116,
        "x1": 0.8028069649577464,
        "y1": 0.3257711684837257
      },
      "text": "As for his sallets, better never was",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5388487887323943,
        "y0": 0.3300544335668966,
        "x1": 0.927901662647888,
        "y1": 0.34941192578969793
      },
      "text": "Then acute sorrell, and sweet three-leav'd grasse, And for a sawee he seldome is at charges.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5388487887323943,
        "y0": 0.3543647954634484,
        "x1": 0.929124294760563,
        "y1": 0.3734822688097495
      },
      "text": "For every crab-tree doth aflfbord him vergis ; His banket sometimes is greene beanes and peason.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5392536338028169,
        "y0": 0.3786166682758621,
        "x1": 0.9497673449014082,
        "y1": 0.3976432916253999
      },
      "text": "Nuts, peares, plumbes, apples, as they are in season. Taijor's Workes, 1630, i. 97-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5194162253521126,
        "y0": 0.40186115804965516,
        "x1": 0.8238572892394367,
        "y1": 0.4246695953475644
      },
      "text": "PESIBLE. Peaceable. {A.-N.) PESIBLETE. A calm. {A.-N.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.42789987684275865,
        "x1": 0.8287194785352111,
        "y1": 0.4380504229337713
      },
      "text": "PESK. A peach. Nominale MS.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.44196038108827596,
        "x1": 0.9497681545915493,
        "y1": 0.4773274348277749
      },
      "text": "PESON. An instrument in the form of a staff, with balls or crockets, used for weighing before scales were employed.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5202259154929577,
        "y0": 0.4814231871875862,
        "x1": 0.7845929852394365,
        "y1": 0.4915737332785988
      },
      "text": "PESS. A hassock. Suffolk.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5202259154929577,
        "y0": 0.49481924413793105,
        "x1": 0.9489568450704225,
        "y1": 0.5312608228092978
      },
      "text": "PESSCOD-SCALDING. A kind of merrymaking in summer evenings ; the treat, green field peas boiled in the shells. Yorksh.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5206307605633802,
        "y0": 0.5349464975324139,
        "x1": 0.7627281126760562,
        "y1": 0.5450970436234264
      },
      "text": "PESSIPE. A kind of cup.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.5487758306358621,
        "x1": 0.8870123105352112,
        "y1": 0.558056280199272
      },
      "text": "PESTERED. Crowded. Peele, ii. 235.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.5618391460510346,
        "x1": 0.9157530717746483,
        "y1": 0.5715163596310312
      },
      "text": "PESTERMENT. Embarrassment. North.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5202259154929577,
        "y0": 0.5753201514331034,
        "x1": 0.9493608804507041,
        "y1": 0.678364807994996
      },
      "text": "PESTLE. (1) A leg of an animal, generally of a pig. A pestle of pork is still in common use. \" Pestels of venison,\" Warner's Antiq. Culin. p. 98. *· Pestell of flesshe,^'amJon,\" Palsgrave. A pestle-pie is a large standing pie which contains a whole gammon, and sometimes a couple of fowls and a neat's tongue, a favorite dish at country fairs, and at Christmas feasts.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5210356056338028,
        "y0": 0.6816552441379311,
        "x1": 0.723858127774648,
        "y1": 0.6927141715552876
      },
      "text": "(2) A constable's staff.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.6950360717241378,
        "x1": 0.8169773521126756,
        "y1": 0.7054772300553697
      },
      "text": "PESTLE-HEAD. A blockhead.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.7097469188813793,
        "x1": 0.7947108732394365,
        "y1": 0.7182164384810635
      },
      "text": "PETE. Pity. See Cov. Myst.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.7242195427048276,
        "x1": 0.8748734359436617,
        "y1": 0.7316371541622412
      },
      "text": "Long lay the kyng, there away wolde not hee",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.7365536723986207,
        "x1": 0.9485503806197186,
        "y1": 0.755208739901262
      },
      "text": "Dayly he propherid batayle : the enmys durst not fyghte Lacke of logynge and vitayle it was grett pete,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.7605590554993105,
        "x1": 0.9485552387605636,
        "y1": 0.7787793682764608
      },
      "text": "Causid the gentill prynce to remeve, siche was Goddes myjte",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5202259154929577,
        "y0": 0.7837902437393103,
        "x1": 0.9473350357183098,
        "y1": 0.8269440384277178
      },
      "text": "Lowe, how the good Lorde his owne gentill knyjte. Because he shulde remcmbir hym in wele and in woo. Thus in every thyng, Lorde, thy wille be doo MS. Bibl. Reg. 17 D. xv.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.8312725911475862,
        "x1": 0.8675813665352108,
        "y1": 0.8402276246096727
      },
      "text": "PETEOSE. Merciful ; compassionate.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5781187605633803,
        "y0": 0.8439340703986207,
        "x1": 0.8522077798309856,
        "y1": 0.8517796165825755
      },
      "text": "Many men spekes of lamentacioun,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5781187605633803,
        "y0": 0.8567444683489654,
        "x1": 0.8882430395492951,
        "y1": 0.8635805298699875
      },
      "text": "OfTmoders and of their gret desolatioun.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6169838873239436,
        "y0": 0.86807035764,
        "x1": 0.831950142197183,
        "y1": 0.8753217421010405
      },
      "text": "Which that thay did indure",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5777139154929577,
        "y0": 0.8789632383944828,
        "x1": 0.8886349295774647,
        "y1": 0.8990323661655919
      },
      "text": "When that their childer dy and passe, But of his peteose tender moder, alasre ·",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6169838873239436,
        "y0": 0.9029406803448277,
        "x1": 0.7522061892957747,
        "y1": 0.9112065973570529
      },
      "text": "I am verray sure.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5777139154929577,
        "y0": 0.9153374769144829,
        "x1": 0.8574610494647885,
        "y1": 0.9229751842337789
      },
      "text": "The wo and payn passis alle otherc.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7845897464788733,
        "y0": 0.9275725537931035,
        "x1": 0.942479323943662,
        "y1": 0.9354034225415274
      },
      "text": "MS. Bodl. e Mils, m<",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
  ],
  "images": [],
  "tables": [],
